=== Methodology note: GPU CLOCK STATE can inflate a result by ~28% ===
  verify.py layer 3, run back-to-back after a benchmark batch:  measured 11.64 (+33%, FAILED)
  same command, same file, GPU settled:                          measured 9.08-9.09 (+4%, PASSED)
  nvidia-smi at the start of the hot run:  1847 MHz.  At the start of the clean run: 936 MHz.
  This is the H3a lesson in the opposite direction - the orphaned-dashboard contention made a
  number look WORSE; a boosted clock makes it look BETTER, which is far more dangerous because
  a flattering result invites no scrutiny.
  CONVENTION UPDATED: log nvidia-smi memory AND clocks.sm before/after every GPU batch, and
  discard any run whose entry clock is boosted relative to the settled idle clock.
